          "path": ".github/scripts/authz_gauntlet_checks.py",
          "line": 46,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "bug",
          "title": "Stop the index matcher at SQL statement boundaries",
          "body": "The `.*?` before `WHERE` crosses semicolons. A valid migration string such as `CREATE INDEX ix ON t (id); DELETE FROM t WHERE expires_at < now()` is consequently reported as containing a volatile index predicate, and the blocking checks reject the PR. Prevent the match from crossing the end of the `CREATE INDEX` statement.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "source_pass": "main"
        },
        {
          "path": ".github/workflows/authz-gauntlet-panel.yml",
          "line": 274,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "security",
          "title": "Restrict Git arguments to preserve the read-only boundary",
          "body": "These permissions allow Git options that write files. For example, `git log -1 --format='...' --output=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/authz-gauntlet-trusted/panel_comment.py\"` can replace the pinned extractor with arbitrary Python, which the subsequent extraction step executes. An injected reviewer instruction can therefore escape the advertised read-only boundary in a job with `id-token: write`. Enforce argument-level restrictions outside the model, including rejecting output-file options, or isolate the reviewer so it cannot modify anything later executed by a privileged step.",
          "confidence": 0.96,
          "source_pass": "main"
        },
        {
          "path": ".github/workflows/authz-gauntlet-panel.yml",
          "line": 268,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "security",
          "title": "Allowed Git commands can overwrite the trusted extractor",
          "body": "The Bash allowlist does not enforce read-only access: `git log` accepts `--output` and an arbitrary `--format`. A prompt injection in the untrusted checkout could induce the reviewer to write Python code into `$RUNNER_TEMP/authz-gauntlet-trusted/panel_comment.py` using those options. The subsequent extraction step executes that file, turning a successful prompt injection into code execution in a job with OIDC permission and access to the review action's credentials. Pinning the extractor and using `python -I` do not protect it from being overwritten.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "source_pass": "security"
        }
      ],
