          "category": "race-condition",
          "title": "Protect task authorization against concurrent RACI edits",
          "body": "`act_on_items` and `sign_off_task` acquire the KPI lock, but `update_close_raci` never acquires that lock, and this RACI read takes no row locks. A reassignment can therefore commit after `_require_owner` authorizes the former Responsible and before their disposal or sign-off commits. The existing RevOps action path prevents this with `lock_raci_for_share`. Coordinate Close RACI writes and task authorization through a shared locking protocol, including Accountable changes through the existing RevOps API.",
          "confidence": 0.96,
          "source_pass": "main"
        }
