          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "security",
          "title": "Concurrent requests can charge the same invoice twice",
          "body": "The prior-payment checks and processor charge are not atomic. Two concurrent requests for the same invoice can both observe no recorded payment and no Braintree transaction, then both call `_charge` before either records its result. This lets an authorized caller charge the customer's full balance multiple times; the modal lock and token expiry do not prevent concurrent API requests, and `orderId` is only used for searching here. Acquire a shared per-invoice lock before the checks and hold it through charging and recording, or atomically reserve the invoice with a durable attempt record that blocks competing requests.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "source_pass": "security"
        }
